From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:36:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/59] net: rfkill: rk: optional gpiod lookups for pins a
 board does not wire

The 6.12 rfkill-wlan and rfkill-bt drivers request every pin with
devm_gpiod_get(), so pins absent from the DT log an error on each boot:
  [WLAN_RFKILL]: rkwlangpiod_request failed to request WIFI,vbat gpio, err -2
  [WLAN_RFKILL]: rkwlangpiod_request failed to request WIFI,reset gpio, err -2
  [BT_RFKILL]: rkgpiod_request failed to request BT,power gpio, err -2
The 6.1 drivers used of_get_named_gpio() and stayed silent.

Use devm_gpiod_get_optional() and return -ENOENT without a message when
the pin is not in the DT; callers see the same return code as before
(bluetooth_platdata_parse_dt() keys on the BT,wake_host result). Wired
pins still log "get property", and -EBUSY (the t4 hog collision) and
every other error still print. 6.12 t6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c   | 8 +++++++-
 net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c b/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c
index ef955de88..edbd85bfd 100644
--- a/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c
+++ b/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c
@@ -564,7 +564,13 @@ static int rkgpiod_request(struct device *dev, const char *con_id,
 	struct  gpio_desc	*gpiodesc;
 	int error;
 
-	gpiodesc = devm_gpiod_get(dev, con_id, flags);
+	gpiodesc = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, con_id, flags);
+	if (!gpiodesc) {
+		/* not wired on this board */
+		DBG("%s no %s gpio\n", __func__, con_id);
+		rk_gpio->io = NULL;
+		return -ENOENT;
+	}
 	error = PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(gpiodesc);
 	if (error) {
 		LOG("%s failed to request %s gpio, err %d\n", __func__, con_id, error);
diff --git a/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c b/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c
index 5d8ea5945..b4dec38ec 100644
--- a/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c
+++ b/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c
@@ -526,7 +526,13 @@ static int rkwlangpiod_request(struct device *dev,
 	struct  gpio_desc	*gpio;
 	int error;
 
-	gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, con_id, flags);
+	gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, con_id, flags);
+	if (!gpio) {
+		/* not wired on this board */
+		DBG("%s no %s gpio\n", __func__, con_id);
+		rk_gpio->io = NULL;
+		return -ENOENT;
+	}
 	error = PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(gpio);
 	if (error) {
 		LOG("%s failed to request %s gpio, err %d\n", __func__, con_id, error);
